# UseCase & ViewModel (Core) — CRITICAL

ViewModels perform data work **only through UseCases**. Never inject Repository into ViewModel.

## UseCase Return Type

Always wrap results in **`UseCaseState`**. Never return raw types or throw for expected failures.

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
suspend operator fun invoke(): List<Category>
suspend operator fun invoke(): List<Category> = repository.getAll() // throws

// ✅ GOOD
suspend operator fun invoke(): UseCaseState<List<Category>> {
    return try {
        when (val result = repository.getAll()) {
            is Result.Success -> UseCaseState.Success(result.data)
            is Result.Error -> UseCaseState.Error(result.error.getMessage())
        }
    } catch (e: Exception) {
        UseCaseState.Error(e.message ?: "Unknown error")
    }
}
```

## ViewModel

```kotlin
// ❌ BAD
internal class CategoryViewModel(
    private val categoryRepository: CategoryRepository,
)

// ✅ GOOD
internal class CategoryViewModel(
    private val getCategoriesUseCase: GetCategoriesUseCase,
) : BaseViewModel<CategoryState, CategoryIntent, CategoryEffect>(savedStateHandle)
```

Handle results via `UseCaseState.Success` / `UseCaseState.Error` — do not rely on uncaught exceptions.
